# Implementation Plan: Comprehensive Google Ads API Integration

Integrate the **Google Ads API** into **Enterprise Meta Leads CRM** (`Leads-CRM`). This integration connects your multi-tenant Node.js/Express backend, Prisma ORM (PostgreSQL), and React frontend with Google Ads to deliver:

1. **OAuth 2.0 Account Connection**: Secure popup-based authorization with encrypted token storage (`refreshTokenEncrypted`).
2. **Inbound Lead Form Webhook**: Direct capture of leads submitted through Google Search & YouTube Lead Form Extensions.
3. **Offline Conversions Upload (OCI & EC4L)**: Automatic feedback loop sending pipeline stage updates (e.g. `Qualified`, `Proposal`, `Won`) back to Google Ads via `gclid` or SHA-256 hashed customer identifiers (`email`, `phone`) to power Smart Bidding.
4. **Google Ads Analytics & ROI Dashboard**: Fetching campaign metrics (`cost_micros`, `clicks`, `impressions`, `conversions`) via Google Ads Query Language (GAQL) and calculating true Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Google Ads Developer Token Access**: Google Ads API requires a Developer Token from a Google Ads Manager Account (MCC). During development and testing, a **Test Access** token can be used with a Google Ads Test Customer ID. For live production deployment, apply for **Basic Access** (15,000 operations/day) in Google Ads API Center.

> [!NOTE]
> **Encryption Key**: Refresh tokens and developer tokens will be encrypted in PostgreSQL using the project's existing AES-256 `ENCRYPTION_KEY` via [utils/encryption.js](file:///b:/Leads-CRM/backend/utils/encryption.js).

