### Backend Core Services & API Layer

#### [NEW] [googleAdsService.js](file:///b:/Leads-CRM/backend/services/googleAdsService.js)
- `getGoogleAdsConfig()`: Retrieves environment client credentials (`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_ADS_REDIRECT_URI`).
- `buildGoogleAdsAuthUrl(organizationId)`: Generates state token via `generateState()` and constructs Google OAuth 2.0 login URL with scope `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords`.
- `handleGoogleAdsCallback(code, state)`: Validates state token, exchanges code for access/refresh tokens, encrypts refresh token, and upserts `GoogleAdsIntegration`.
- `uploadOfflineConversion({ organizationId, lead, conversionActionId, value })`:
  - Uploads click conversion via Google Ads API (`google-ads-api` SDK or Google REST API).
  - Uses `gclid` if available.
  - Automatically falls back to **Enhanced Conversions for Leads (EC4L)** with SHA-256 hashed `email` and `phone` if `gclid` is missing.
- `fetchCampaignPerformance(organizationId)`: Executes GAQL query to retrieve campaign spend (`cost_micros`), clicks, impressions, and conversions.
- `getGoogleAdsConfigSummary(organizationId)`, `updateGoogleAdsConfig(organizationId, payload)`, `disconnectGoogleAds(organizationId)`.

#### [NEW] [googleAdsRoutes.js](file:///b:/Leads-CRM/backend/routes/googleAdsRoutes.js)
- `GET /api/google-ads/callback`: Public callback endpoint called by Google during OAuth popup flow. Uses `renderPopupResponse()` from `popupHelper.js`.
- Protected Admin Routes:
  - `GET /api/google-ads/auth-url`: Generates OAuth login URL.
  - `GET /api/google-ads/config`: Returns integration status, Customer ID, and stage mapping.
  - `POST /api/google-ads/config`: Saves Customer ID, Developer Token, and conversion stage mapping.
  - `POST /api/google-ads/disconnect`: Disconnects Google Ads integration.
  - `GET /api/google-ads/campaigns`: Returns live Google Ads campaign analytics.
  - `POST /api/google-ads/test-conversion`: Triggers a test conversion event.

